.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_TIME_CMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_time_cmp ,
.Nm dtfl_time_less_equal ,
.Nm dtfl_time_less_than ,
.Nm dtfl_time_minimum ,
.Nm dtfl_time_join ,
.Nm dtfl_time_meet
.Nd order and lattice operations on times
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/time.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_time_cmp "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const uint64_t *a" "const uint64_t *b"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_time_less_equal "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const uint64_t *a" "const uint64_t *b"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_time_less_than "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const uint64_t *a" "const uint64_t *b"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_time_minimum "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "uint64_t *out"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_time_join "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const uint64_t *a" "const uint64_t *b" "uint64_t *out"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_time_meet "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const uint64_t *a" "const uint64_t *b" "uint64_t *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each function takes times of class
.Fa tc ,
as arrays of
.Fn dtfl_time_depth tc
words.
A time has two orders, as in Rust.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_time_cmp
is the total order Rust's derived
.Vt Ord
gives the timestamp type, and returns a negative, zero or positive
value.
For every class it is the lexicographic order of the words, so it is
used to sort and deduplicate times.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_time_less_equal
is the partial order of timely's
.Vt PartialOrder ,
which decides progress.
.Fn dtfl_time_less_than
is
.Fn dtfl_time_less_equal
for distinct times.
If
.Fa a
is less than or equal to
.Fa b
in the partial order, then
.Fn dtfl_time_cmp
of them is not positive.
Per class:
.Bl -tag -width POINTSTAMP
.It unit
always true.
.It total, AltNeu
numeric order of the value (for AltNeu, of (time, neu)).
.It product
both halves less or equal.
.It lex
the first halves are strictly less, or equal with the second halves
less or equal.
.It PointStamp
every coordinate less or equal, with missing coordinates the minimum.
.El
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_time_minimum
stores the least time of the class.
.Fn dtfl_time_join
stores the least upper bound of
.Fa a
and
.Fa b ,
and
.Fn dtfl_time_meet
the greatest lower bound, as differential dataflow's
.Vt Lattice .
Totals take the maximum and minimum, products and PointStamps work
coordinate by coordinate.
For a lex class whose first halves are incomparable, the join is
(first join, second minimum) and the meet is (first meet, second
maximum).
.Fa out
may be the same array as
.Fa a
or
.Fa b .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_time_cmp
returns a negative value, 0, or a positive value as
.Fa a
is less than, equal to, or greater than
.Fa b .
.Fn dtfl_time_less_equal
and
.Fn dtfl_time_less_than
return the comparison.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Product times (3, 7) and (4, 6) are incomparable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint64_t a[2] = { 3, 7 }, b[2] = { 4, 6 }, j[2], m[2];

dtfl_time_less_equal(tc, a, b);	/* false */
dtfl_time_cmp(tc, a, b);	/* negative */
dtfl_time_join(tc, a, b, j);	/* (4, 7) */
dtfl_time_meet(tc, a, b, m);	/* (3, 6) */
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
None.
The arrays must hold a whole time of the class; nothing checks.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_summary_results_in 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_time_class 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are timely-dataflow's
.Vt PartialOrder
(timely/src/order.rs) and differential-dataflow's
.Vt Lattice
(differential-dataflow/src/lattice.rs), at the pins.
Rust keeps
.Vt Ord
and
.Vt PartialOrder
apart for the same reason this API does: sorting needs a total order,
and progress needs the partial one.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
All of these are pure functions of their arguments, safe to call from
any thread.
